# HB-2026-004
## Date Completed: September 22, 2026
## Priority:  Critical
## Category: Customer Support PC dead

### Problem: 
Customer Support desktop won't turn on, says no lights, no fan, nothing is happening when the power button is pressed. Customer Support agent was unable to access the computer or take calls, cauing calls to queue without an available agent.  

### Troubleshooting Process: 
1. Confirmed the desktop was completely unresponsive when the power button was pressed. 
2. Confirmed with the customer that the wall outlet was functional and the power cord was not the source of the issue.
3. Reviewed the hardware and asset documentation for Customer Support individuals to identify the appropriate replacement workstation process.
4. Navigated to Tools -> Computer Deployment and began preparing a replacement workstation.
5. Confirmed with the customer that the replacement device needed to be a desktop rather than a laptop.
6. Used appropriate server imaging process to build and configure the replacement desktop according to the Customer Support hardware documentation. 
7. Completed server imaging and prepared the replacement workstation for shipment.
8. Contacted the customer to obtain their mailing address.
9. Processed the replacement workstation for shipment to the customer. 

### Resolution: 
The Customer Support desktop was determined to require replacement so a replacement desktop was built using the appropriate server imagine process and prepared for shipment. The replacement was shipped to the customer at the provided mailing address so they could return to normal operations. 

### Status: 
Resolved
